        Markdown("To go further:\n\n- Read the language properly, starting at [Language basics](/learn/04-language-basics).\n- Talk to a real server: [Data and APIs](/learn/15-data).\n- Make the site work offline: [Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline).\n- Translate it: [Translate a site](/recipes/translate-a-site).\n- Build a bigger project: [Tutorials](/learn/03-tutorial-todos).")

        Heading("Common mistakes", id: "common-mistakes").h2

        Markdown("Reading a value that may be missing. `books.find(…)` finds nothing when no book has the slug, so `book` is a `Book?`:")

        CodeBlock(#"type Book { slug: String, title: String }

const books: [Book] = [Book(slug: "a-pattern-language", title: "A Pattern Language")]

page BookPage(path: "/books/:slug", slug: String, title: "Book", description: "One book.") {
    derived book = books.find(b => b.slug == slug)
    Heading(book.title).h1
}"#, title: "wf · draws T04")

        Markdown("Bind it with `if let b = book \{ Heading(b.title).h1 \}`, as step 5 does, or read it as `book?.title ?? \"Book\"` ([T04](/errors/T04)).\n\nA field the type does not have. `type Book` names every field, so a typo is an error where it is written:")

        CodeBlock(#"type Book { slug: String, title: String }

const books: [Book] = [Book(slug: "a-pattern-language", title: "A Pattern Language")]

page Home(path: "/", title: "Shelf", description: "Books worth reading.") {
    Heading("Books").h1
    for book in books by book.slug {
        Text(book.titel)
    }
}"#, title: "wf · draws T05")

        Markdown("Use the name the message suggests, `book.title` ([T05](/errors/T05)).\n\nA store member the store does not declare. `Shelf` has `saved`, `count` and `toggle`, and nothing else:")

        CodeBlock(#"store Shelf {
    persist saved: [String] = []
    action toggle(slug: String) {
        saved = if saved.includes(slug) { saved.filter(s => s != slug) } else { [...saved, slug] }
    }
}

page Home(path: "/", title: "Shelf", description: "Books worth reading.") {
    use Shelf
    Heading("Books").h1
    Text("{Shelf.total} saved")
    Button("Keep it") { on click { Shelf.toggle("a-pattern-language") } }
}"#, title: "wf · draws T06")

        Markdown("Read a member the store declares, or declare the one you need: `derived count = saved.length` ([T06](/errors/T06)).\n\nGoing further: if you know React, Vue or Svelte, [Coming from React, Vue or Svelte](/coming-from/react) maps what you know onto WebFluent.")
    }
}
